.Dd $Mdocdate$
.Dt TRIAGE 5
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm triage
.Nd triage.yaml configuration file format
.Sh DESCRIPTION
A
.Pa triage.yaml
file declares environment prerequisites for a project — tools,
versions, env vars, files, platform-guarded commands, and cross-repo delegation.
.Pp
This page documents the file format.
For the CLI surface, see
.Xr triage 1 .
.Pp
The canonical prose source is
.Pa specs/config.md
in the source repository; this page is a hand-authored reference distilled
from it.
.Sh FILE STRUCTURE
Root is always a mapping.
Checks live under profile keys — never at the root.
.Pp
Config file names (discovery order):
.Pa triage.yaml ,
.Pa triage.yml ,
.Pa .triage.yaml ,
.Pa .triage.yml .
One entry file per run; no parent-directory walk-up unless you pass an explicit
path to
.Xr triage 1 .
.Sh PROFILES
.Bl -tag -width default -compact
.It Sy default
Profile run when
.Fl -profile
is omitted.
May be omitted (treated as empty).
.It Ar name
Any other top-level key (except
.Sy include
and
.Sy vars )
is a profile name — e.g.\&
.Sy release ,
.Sy ci .
Select with
.Fl -profile Ar name
on
.Xr triage 1 .
.El
.Pp
Profile value is either:
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
A check list.
.It
.Ql { extends: [profiles\[u2026]], add: [checks\[u2026]] }
when inheriting.
Use
.Sy add
(not
.Sy checks )
with
.Sy extends .
.El
.Sh COMPOSITION
Two axes — separate mechanisms:
.Bl -tag -width extends -compact
.It Sy include
Top-level list of YAML files merged in order.
Collisions emit load-time warnings; later wins.
.It Sy extends
Per-profile inheritance within the merged config.
Same collision rules.
.El
.Sh VARS
Top-level
.Sy vars
mapping of reusable strings.
Reference in check fields with
.Sy {{ var_name }} .
.Pp
Precedence: config
.Sy vars
< CLI
.Fl -var
< built-ins
.Pq Sy profile , Sy os .
.Pp
Expansion is fail-closed on undefined or malformed tokens.
Vars are not recursive.
.Sh CHECK TYPES
Each check uses a type-as-key entry.
Optional fields apply to any check unless noted.
.Sh COMMON FIELDS
.Bl -tag -width platform -compact
.It Sy severity
.Sy error ,
.Sy warn ,
or
.Sy info
(default
.Sy error ) .
.It Sy platform
.Sy macos ,
.Sy linux ,
or
.Sy windows
— string or list; skip on non-matching OS.
.It Sy hint
Remediation text on failure.
.It Sy dir
Working directory (default: config directory).
.It Sy serial
Opt out of concurrent execution for this check or group.
.El
.Ss tool
Command present on
.Pa PATH .
Optional version constraint (pick one):
.Bl -tag -width version_from -compact
.It Sy version
npm-style semver range, quoted in YAML
.Pq e.g.\& Ql ">=1.26" .
.It Sy version_from
Read pin from a file
.Pq e.g.\& Pa .go-version .
.El
.Bd -literal -offset indent
- tool: go
  version_from: .go-version
  hint: https://go.dev/dl
.Ed
.Ss env
Environment variable presence or absence.
.Bl -tag -width unset -compact
.It Cm env\&: Ar VAR
Variable must be present (default).
Optional
.Sy matches
regex on value.
.It Cm unset\&: Li true
Variable must not be in the environment.
Mutually exclusive with
.Sy matches .
.El
.Ss path
File or directory must exist.
Globs supported.
Relative paths resolve from
.Sy dir
or config directory.
.Ss one_of
At least one alternative must pass — either tool names or sub-checks:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
- one_of: [pnpm, npm]
- one_of:
    - env: SOPS_AGE_KEY
    - path: ~/.config/sops/age/keys.txt
.Ed
.Ss command
Run an explicitly-interpreted snippet.
Requires
.Sy label .
No implicit shell —
.Sy interp
selects
.Sy sh
or
.Sy pwsh
(default
.Sy sh ) .
.Pp
Assertions: exit 0 (default),
.Sy contains ,
.Sy matches ,
or
.Sy exit .
Optional
.Sy with_env
map for this command only.
.Bd -literal -offset indent
- command: security find-identity -v -p codesigning
  label: Apple Distribution certificate
  contains: Apple Distribution
  platform: macos
.Ed
.Ss delegate
Load and run a child config in-process.
Required
.Sy dir ;
optional
.Sy config
(default
.Pa triage.yaml
under
.Sy dir ) .
Active profile is forwarded.
Nested delegates allowed; cycles are config errors.
.Bd -literal -offset indent
- delegate: vitalink-api
  dir: vitalink-api
.Ed
.Ss group
Named container;
.Sy items
holds child checks and nested groups.
Optional
.Sy platform
skips the whole section on non-matching OS.
.Bd -literal -offset indent
- group: Core toolchain
  items:
    - tool: git
    - tool: go
      version_from: .go-version
.Ed
.Sh SEVERITY
Orthogonal to profile — profile selects which checks run;
severity decides how failures are treated.
.Bl -tag -width warn -compact
.It Sy error
Required; fails the run (default).
.It Sy warn
Recommended; shows [!] but does not fail unless
.Fl -strict
on
.Xr triage 1 .
.It Sy info
FYI only.
.El
.Pp
.Cm required\&: Li true|false
sugar
.Pq Sy true No -> Sy error , Sy false No -> Sy warn .
.Sh EXAMPLES
Single-profile repo:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
default:
  - tool: git
  - tool: go
    version_from: .go-version
  - tool: golangci-lint
    severity: warn
    hint: brew install golangci-lint
.Ed
.Pp
Multi-profile with inheritance:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
include:
  - base.yaml

default:
  - tool: go
    version_from: .go-version

release:
  extends: [default]
  add:
    - tool: sops
      hint: brew install sops
.Ed
.Pp
Workspace with delegation:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
default:
  - delegate: api
    dir: api
  - command: make doctor MODE={{profile}}
    label: legacy-web
    dir: legacy-web
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr triage 1
.Pq Sy man 1 triage
.Pp
.Pa specs/config.md
in the source repository — full config reference in prose.
.Pp
.Pa schema/triage.schema.json
— JSON Schema for editor validation.
.Pp
.Lk https://github.com/lolay/triage/tree/main/examples "Worked example configs"
